# Used by Dockerfile.mapproxy (context .). An allowlist: everything is left
# out of the build context except the files the Dockerfile COPYs (the two
# mapproxy/conda-*.lock files, mapproxy/docker/app.py and
# mapproxy/docker/mesh_guard.py). A list of what to exclude never keeps up
# with the repository -- site/, site-docs/, images/ and a local .venv/ are
# all large and were all being sent to the Docker daemon on every build --
# whereas a new file the image needs fails the build at once with
# "not found".
#
# Add a `!path` line here whenever Dockerfile.mapproxy gets a new COPY.
# Bind-mounted at Compose runtime, never copied into an image: the MBTiles
# under tileserver/data (hundreds of GB, which would stall the upload),
# tileserver/{config,fonts,styles}, mapproxy/{config,data,locks,tile_locks}
# and nginx.
*
!mapproxy/conda-linux-64.lock
!mapproxy/conda-linux-aarch64.lock
!mapproxy/docker/app.py
!mapproxy/docker/mesh_guard.py
